      "content": "The correct order of bond dissociation enthalpy of halogens is :",
      "options": [
        {
          "identifier": "A",
          "content": "F<sub>2</sub> &gt; Cl<sub>2</sub> &gt; Br<sub>2</sub> &gt; I<sub>2</sub>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "B",
          "content": "Cl<sub>2</sub> &gt; Br<sub>2</sub> &gt; F<sub>2</sub> &gt; I<sub>2</sub>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "C",
          "content": "I<sub>2</sub> &gt; Br<sub>2</sub> &gt; Cl<sub>2</sub> &gt; F<sub>2</sub>"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "D",
          "content": "Cl<sub>2</sub> &gt; F<sub>2</sub> &gt; Br<sub>2</sub> &gt; I<sub>2</sub>"
        }
      ],
      "correct_options": [
        "B"
      ],
      "explanation": "<p>Among halogens (F<sub>2</sub>, Cl<sub>2</sub>, Br<sub>2</sub> and I<sub>2</sub>), bond dissociation enthalpy (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.885ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 833 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><sub>diss</sub>H<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"0.988ex\" height=\"1.532ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 436.6 677\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(33,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2218\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2218\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) of I<sub>2</sub>, is minimum because of larger size of I-atom there is a steric repulsion between bonded I-atoms, which makes I-I bond weakest.</p>\n<p>Whereas, smaller size and highest electronegativity of F-atom cause highest electron density on F-atom of F<sub>2</sub> molecule. As a result, F-F bond becomes weaker due to electrostatic repulsion between bonded F-atoms.</p>\n<p>Thus, the order of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.885ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 833 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\